{% set local_problem %}
<p>Decatur's river location creates gutter challenges you won't find in other North Alabama cities. The Tennessee River wraps around your city, Wheeler Lake sits nearby, and constant humidity hangs in the air. That's a perfect recipe for gutter problems — and the consequences of neglect are more severe here than anywhere else we serve.</p>

<p>Start with the debris. Yes, you have local trees dropping leaves and pine needles like everywhere else. But Decatur also gets wind-blown organic matter from the river system — leaves, seed pods, pollen, and particulates that travel miles on the breeze. Even homes with minimal tree coverage find their gutters filling with debris blown in from elsewhere.</p>

<p>Then there's the humidity factor. In most of North Alabama, leaves in gutters dry out and can be scooped easily. In Decatur's muggy river air, those leaves decompose into thick, composted sludge within weeks. That muck is harder to remove, holds moisture against your gutters and fascia, and creates the perfect breeding ground for mosquitoes and mold.</p>

<p>The consequences are immediate. When gutters overflow during Decatur's intense storms, that water lands right next to your foundation — which is already dealing with pressure from a naturally high water table. You're adding water to soil that's often already saturated from below. Foundation damage, basement moisture, and landscape erosion follow.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set service_explanation %}
<p>Our gutter cleaning service is comprehensive — and designed for Decatur's specific conditions. We start by hand-removing all debris from inside your gutters: leaves, pine needles, river-blown organics, decomposed sludge, and roof grit. We don't just blow debris onto your lawn or push it toward the downspouts.</p>

<p>In Decatur's humid climate, we pay special attention to the sludge that builds up at the bottom of gutters. This decomposed organic matter holds moisture against the gutter bottom, accelerating corrosion. We clear it completely, not just the visible debris on top.</p>

<p>Next, we flush all downspouts with water to ensure they're clear and flowing properly. Downspout clogs are common when wet debris builds up — and in Decatur, that debris stays wet longer than elsewhere. We verify water exits at the bottom, not just that it enters at the top.</p>

<p>Finally, we inspect your entire gutter system with an eye toward humidity damage: rust developing at seams, loose hangers, fascia showing early signs of rot, and any gaps that could let water behind the gutters. We'll flag problems before they become expensive repairs.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set why_us %}
<p>We've been cleaning gutters throughout Morgan County for over 20 years — long enough to understand what the Tennessee River does to homes here. Decatur isn't the same as Huntsville or Madison. The humidity is higher, the debris is different, and the consequences of clogged gutters are more severe.</p>

<p>We bring the right equipment, the experience to work safely and efficiently, and the local knowledge to understand Decatur's unique challenges. When you call Blue River Gutters, you're getting professionals who know your city and care about doing the job right.</p>
